  data: {
    LLM: 'Players take turns playing one card face-up to the center pile. When a face card or Ace is played, the next player must play a face card within a set number of turns or forfeit their pile to the face-card player:\n- Ace: 4 chances\n- King: 3 chances\n- Queen: 2 chances\n- Jack: 1 chance\nIf they play a face card: the challenge passes forward.',
    Player: 'Players take turns playing one card face-up to the center pile. When a face card or Ace is played, the next player must play a face card within a set number of turns or forfeit their pile to the face-card player:\n- Ace: 4 chances\n- King: 3 chances\n- Queen: 2 chances\n- Jack: 1 chance\nIf they play a face card: the challenge passes forward.',
    objective: 'Collect all 52 cards by winning the central pile through valid slaps (on doubles, sandwiches, sequences, etc.) and by claiming the pile when opponents fail to counter face-card challenges.',
    gameplay: 'Players take turns playing one card face-up to the center pile. When a face card or Ace is played, the next player must play a face card within a set number of turns or forfeit their pile to the face-card player:\n- Ace: 4 chances\n- King: 3 chances\n- Queen: 2 chances\n- Jack: 1 chance\nIf they play a face card: the challenge passes forward.',
    keyRules: [
      'When a player runs out of cards, they may still slap back in.',
      'If a player false-slaps and has fewer than 2 cards, they are eliminated.',
      'Only designated slap conditions are valid (house rules vary widely).',
    ],
